A||N||25||Monkeyman||I hate deer!!!||||8||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||05-27-2001||05:32 AM||||Stupid deer!  One just decided to attack my GT a couple of hours ago.  From what I can tell here's what he/she damaged.  Front fascia has a nice crack in the corner, passenger mirror was broken off (easy to fix), passenger side door skin has some deep gouges, antenna was broken off (mounting bolt, too), and (this is the worst according to my wallet) the windshield is cracked.  I need to find some cheap ways of fixing some of these since I have a $500 deductable.  Most of the things I can fix myself (with new parts, of course), but I can't do the windshield.  Anyone have any idea how much it should cost to have the windshield replaced (weatherstrip around windshield, too)?  I did a search but didn't come up with the info I was looking for.<P>Thanx in advance.  (BTW--I hope that frigging deer has a hell of a headache! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">)<P>MM||||reg||8
Z||000001||Old Lar||05-27-2001||06:25 AM||||Sorry about Bambi meets monkeyman.. a windshield is around $150. If you want to keep it stock looking, keep the small size gasket or they are more than likely to install a wider windshield gasket.||||reg||3
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-27-2001||07:38 AM||||the oem molding isnt avail anymore. some use an aftermarket one now that doesnt wrap behind the glass. Save and use the oem one. The aftermarkey one on mine eased out in hot summer sun and blew off. There is an aftermarket one that does wrap around. that what they replaced mine with this time, but it is slightly wider than oem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||05-27-2001||09:50 AM||||Sorry about what happened. As for the windshield, We bought one from a local club memeber ($80) and installed it ourselves. Changing a windshield isn't that hard. Took us about 2 hours. There are 2 tools for taking out windshields. 1 is a wire saw type, the other is an "L" shaped blade tool. We used the "L" shaped one and it took 20 minutes to remove the old one. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||05-27-2001||10:08 AM||||Hey MM!<BR>I have a spare windshield, you close to Grand Rapids, Michigan?<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||05-27-2001||10:59 AM||||anyone know ow to put a winsheild in a Fiero? I use to replace my own on vws, and it was very easy, all you needed was a thin piece of rope that went all around the windsheild weatherstrip, put some talcom poweder on it, one person held the windsheild against the opening while another got inside the car and pulled both ends of the rope at the same time.<P>  as the rope pulled off the weatherstripping lip, it pulled the lip into the frame.  Took about 2 milutes to put one in - the hardest part was transferring the stickers.<P>   I dont know how a fiero windsheild goes in, but if its similar...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||05-27-2001||11:10 AM||||Ken--The windshield is glued into a Fiero.  The trim is decorative only (basically--it does help to keep the edges of the glass from chipping).  In a VW, the trim/moulding actually holds the windshield in place.<P>I think I'll have a professional replace the windshield since I only intend to buy one (I'm not very mechanical).  If they break it, they get to buy me a new one.<P>Hopefully, the insurance company will settle right.  I'm sure they'll tell me that they can find someone to fix the split in my fascia, but I won't let them do that.  I'll insist on another unsplit fascia.  I'd hate for the repair to split open in the future.  Progressive is soooooo cheap.  I think it's time to find another insurance carrier.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000007||grinthock||05-27-2001||11:34 AM||||I was HIT by a deer while travelling at 50mph about 2 years ago scared the living SH1T out of me!||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||05-27-2001||11:58 AM||||DONT USE SAFTY-LITE they suck those idiots made a mess of my windshield and screwed up the weather strip, when I went back to complain about it they tried to say it was sunroof that was making all the noise. After a call to the main HQ they offered to replace it for free well dont you know they screwed it up again! <BR>What they were doing is setting the glass to low in the frame causing a big lip at the top of the glass thus causing wind noise.Any idiot with half a brain could see the windshield was not flush with the roof. I finally went to someone else and they did it right the first time, yeah another 140 bucks but they threw in the trim for free  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>It's interesting to note that my windshield has a compound curve at the top. Apparently PPG did some kind of modification to it where a normal stock glass has a curve only from left to right and is realitvly flat top to bottom, mine has a noticable curve at the top as well. Just food for thaught.||||reg||4
Z||000009||phreakboy4||05-27-2001||03:34 PM||||when I got my fiero I had Diamond glass install one it cost me 116.00 dollars and hasnt leaked they came to where the car was at and had it changed it less the 15 mins. I know they are pretty much all over the states so their just might be one near you. They also have a website that you could get quotes off of.<P>        Phreakboy45@cs.com         Sean V<P>     <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||05-27-2001||04:31 PM||||The insurance adjuster just left a little while ago.  Turns out the GT is probably going to be totalled.  What idiots (must be related to Bambi).  There's no way it will cost more to fix it than it's worth.  I've tossed around the idea of getting a fastback for a while now.  I guess this is my opportunity.  No matter which way the insurance goes, I'll end up with a little bit of money.  Once I get my GT sold (see my thread in "The Mall"), I should have enough for a decent fastback.  (I know.  I've always been a notchback kind of guy, but...)  If anybody sees a slightly damaged deer around north central Indiana, please give her a hard kick for me. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroJoe||05-27-2001||07:12 PM||||Well, if it makes you feel any better, I ate venison tonight for dinner...maybe my 8 point I got this year was related to yours  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Max The Chainsaw||05-28-2001||12:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>I was HIT by a deer while travelling at 50mph about 2 years ago scared the living SH1T out of me!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Damn, a few years ago my wife, a friend and I were traveling thru Rankin IL at 5 AM. Saw another car coming toward us with a flickering in the headlights (55 MPH). Both cars met in a herd of 6 or more deer. Wife screamed, friend hit the rear floorboard (coward....). To this day I still don't know how we managed to get thru there without hitting the other car or any of those deer. Yeah, it scares the Sh1t out of you for sure!!<P>Sorry to hear about your GT Monkeyman, that is a nice looking GT. BTW, got the old Grape Ape almost restored, just waiting for it to come back from the paint shop. (Purple metalliac.... )   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||GoCartGuy||05-29-2001||01:41 AM||||Had a similar experience Monkey.  Was driving home doin about 45 and she came from the right, slamming into my little GoCart.  Anyways, I had to replace the front panel over the wheel, the passenger mirror, the windshield, and fix a crack in both the rear quarter panel and the spoiler.  Total damage, about $1200. Thank god for good insurance, USAA with a $100 deductable.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ken Wittlief||05-29-2001||09:32 AM||||The thing that really sucks about hitting a deer in a Fiero is you have such a small forward profile, exceptional handling, and low roof line that we should have the lowests probibilty of hitting a deer.<P>  They should be able to jump over a fiero  with about as much effort as it takes a human to jump over a curb with a running start and Air Nikes.<P>  One thing I recommend - make sure you have halogen lamps in your headlights so you can see better, and if you do round a bend and see deer in the  road, if at all possible kill your headlights and lean on the horn, while braking and steering behind them (thats 4 things at once isnt it?)<P>  they really do go fixated on your headlights and will stand there and stare at you.<P>  When they run out from the side into your path there really isnt much you can do about it. Be glad your windshild is sloped back at 60°, and not at 89° like they are on a VW bug - at least your car will slide under them.||||reg||1
Z||000015||wkayl||05-29-2001||10:02 AM||||Did it look like this just before you said s***.  This was taken a year ago in the northern Black Hills of S Dak.  I was driving about 15 mph because I knew there were many deer. <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deerthree_1.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 05-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||84Bill||05-29-2001||10:47 AM||||Totaled? Sheesh well I guess if the damage exceeds the replacement cost then it is a total loss. I have found that some insurence Co's are totaling Fieros just to get them off the road. I have no idea why they are doing this. <BR>There is special insurance we can get for our cars since they were a unique limited production car and are no longer being produced. A good idea is to ask what the insurance co will do if your car is badly damaged. <BR>I know my 84 qualifies for this type of insurance now It also can be tagged as a "classic" car BUT I would not be able to daily drive it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/sig.jpg"> ||||reg||11
Z||000017||StuGood||05-29-2001||03:12 PM||||As Homer would say, "Doe-!"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Sorry to learn of your accident.  I'm glad the car sustained damage, instead of you.  <P>FWIW, I had Triumph Auto Glass replace a cracked windshield in my 1988 Fiero (was cracked when I bought the car) about a year ago, and it cost something less than $150 (I forget the exact cost, but a cheap car payment in any case!).  They did all the work, it looks fine, and it hasn't leaked even in heavy rainstorms.   ||||reg||11
Z||000018||Monkeyman||05-29-2001||05:44 PM||||Got word from the insurance company today.  They totalled it.  I'll be buying it back, of course.  I'll get a small check from them and still get to sell the car so I actually came out about even.  Still time for another Fiero, though.  Now I just have to think of a name for the upcoming GT.  Since it'll be my 4th Fiero, my wife (the pervert) thought of "4Play".  Hmm...<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000019||Raydar||05-29-2001||06:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>"4Play".  Hmm...<P>MM</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I like it!<P>Sorry to hear about your close encounter of the four-legged kind. Glad you didn't get a lapful of deer, though. That could have given you a <I>really</I> bad day.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000020||Mach10||05-29-2001||08:23 PM||||I hit a deer once. Cute little Doe, comes barrelling out of the ditch, right in front of my car. I hit the brakes, she jumps back into the ditch, out of sight. I back off the brakes, just in time to see the stupid beast come flying BACK ONTO THE ROAD. She had enough time to jump STRAIGHT UP before my bumper caught her hind legs. She rolled up my hood and off before reaching the glass, and I heard a double-thunk as she kicked my door in on the way down. Hits the ground, rolls, gets up, and streaks off.<BR>Some old guy was watching this, busting a gut. I get out to see 2 neat dents in my door. Could have been much worse. My cousin was HIT BY A DEER around christmas last year. The stupid animal t-boned him, smashing the glass, and head-butting his girlfriend. Not pretty. He showed up late to the party on account of driving his girlfriend to the hospital for 4 stitches. Not cool.||||reg||6
