Z||000023||rogergarrison||05-30-2001||08:33 AM||||totalled is not always a bad thing. If its still drivable and not too bad, take the money and theyll sell it back to you for almost nothing. I had a gf wreck her Volvo. Just messed up fender, grill, lites, hood nothing mechanical, parts were so expensive they totalled it. Gave her $5000. She paid off the loan, bought it back from insurance company for $200. I bought parts used and fixed it and repainted it for $1800. So she still had her car, better than it was, paid for and made a couple thousand cash to boot.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Monkeyman||05-30-2001||12:48 PM||||That's basically what's happening here.  The damage is really minimal (even replacing the windshield is relatively cheap), totally cosmetic and I could probably fix most of the damage myself.  Unfortunately, I just don't have the time to mess with it.  That's one of the reasons I'm selling it as cheaply as I am.  There are a number of forum members who have driven the car and can attest to the strength and reliability of it.  If I fixed everything that's now wrong and had it repainted, I could surely get at least 3 grand out of it and not spend any where near a grand getting it done, just some elbow grease.  This will make someone a nice ride.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000025||TSPalmer||05-30-2001||01:29 PM||||MM, sorry to hear about your deer incident.  I drove through a covey of quail right after dusk and totally removed the windshield from a Fiat X1/9. Not fun at all.<P>"4Play" rules, good luck on getting it!||||reg||6
